  "presentation_summary": [
    "Sixty-seven-year-old woman with asthma, hypertension, urinary incontinence, obesity, and no personal or family history of anesthesia complications underwent elective hysterectomy.",
    "Preoperative values included temperature 36.8 C, BP 148/78 mmHg, RR 26/min, WBC 11.19 K/mcL, hemoglobin 13.5 g/dL, hematocrit 43.9%, platelets 314 K/mcL, sodium 140 mmol/L, potassium 4.6 mmol/L, chloride 100 mmol/L, bicarbonate 25 mmol/L, anion gap 20, glucose 130 mg/dL, BUN 15 mg/dL, creatinine 0.72 mg/dL, eGFR 92, and calcium 9.1 mg/dL.",
    "Induction included fentanyl, lidocaine, propofol, succinylcholine 1 mg/kg, jaw stiffness during intubation, rocuronium, and sevoflurane maintenance.",
    "During the first hour MAP stayed 60 to 65 mmHg and EtCO2 was 34 to 36 mmHg with RR 12/min and tidal volume 500 mL.",
    "At 4 hours temperature rose to 38.3 C and EtCO2 to 51 mmHg despite increased ventilation; 45 minutes later temperature was 38.8 C and EtCO2 58 mmHg despite RR 20/min, tidal volume 600 mL, high fresh gas flow, FiO2 80%, and equipment checks.",
    "ABG showed pH 7.22, PaCO2 58 mmHg, PaO2 237 mmHg, base excess -4.7, bicarbonate 23.8 mmol/L, lactate 5.3 mmol/L, potassium 5.4 mmol/L, and ionized calcium 4.5 mg/dL.",
    "Sevoflurane was stopped, FiO2 was increased to 100%, total intravenous anesthesia was started, dantrolene 2.5 mg/kg was repeated after 8 minutes, cooling and metabolic/electrolyte treatment were given, hypotension was treated with epinephrine and phenylephrine, and the surgery was aborted after stabilization.",
    "Within 25 minutes temperature was 37.0 C and EtCO2 37 mmHg. Discharge labs included CK 2518 U/L and potassium 4.1 mmol/L on postoperative day 7."
  ],
